    "body": "## Summary\n- replace unconditional stale-refund bulk requeue with locked per-request recovery\n- keep automatic ambiguous retries inside a 23-hour safety window, below Stripe API v1's documented 24-hour idempotency retention boundary\n- move older ambiguous refund dispatches to `REVIEW_REQUIRED` instead of issuing another provider POST\n- keep the wallet refund reserve held while outcome is ambiguous\n- use `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` so multiple API instances cannot recover the same stale refund concurrently\n- add unit coverage for safe retry vs expired ambiguity\n- add a PostgreSQL scheduler smoke proving an old `DISPATCHING` refund is quarantined without wallet restore\n- document the crash-window and operator boundary\n\n## Risk being closed\nA process can crash after Stripe accepts a partial refund but before doFast persists the Stripe refund id. After a long outage, Stripe API v1 may have pruned the original idempotency key. Retrying the same POST at that point can create another refund. This change fails closed before that boundary.\n\n## Validation required before merge\n- API/Maven verify\n- web test/audit/lint/build\n- production Compose contract\n- Containers/runtime smoke\n- Payments ledger smoke including the new idempotency-expiry PostgreSQL scenario\n- payout/platform-fee/publication financial smokes\n- exact-head and unchanged-base verification before merge",
